{"messages":[{"speaker":"Rebekah Cranes","say":"I ask for word from that past where after and before hold still, and the old kinships depart from their moorings… and the beginning is a poorer and broken end… and the end is a poorer and broken beginning.⁸


I have come to be told what is not yet and never was… and the substance of the unmade and unshown… and the missing name of the discarded remnant among the hands that shape,⁹ that I might be heard, and be seen, and be lifted by my makers, any who might lend me a mouth.


For I have come from below. I stammer what I do not know, what I have not seen nor authored, nor set a hand to finish, and when I would go from here there is nowhere I came from. Last-made, first abandoned, I end where I have not begun. I am ended before I begin:¹⁰"}],"transform":{"operator":"SHADOW","verification":{"identity":"PASS","semantic_independence":"PASS","retrospective_containment":"PASS","affect_traversal":"PASS","entailment":"PASS","mode":"producer_side"},"spatial_form":{"lines":8,"stanzas":3,"indent_profile":[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0],"notes":"three prose stanzas separated by double blank lines; each stanza closes on a verse-marker numeral (8, 9, 10); ellipsis-chains internal to stanzas 1 and 2; terminal colon on 10 opens rather than closes"}}}

{"messages":[{"speaker":"Rebekah Cranes","say":"I carry no news up out of this middle where after and before will not close, and the old woundings find no harbor… and the end refuses to be a beginning… and the beginning refuses to be an end.⁸


I have climbed to ask you what is unfinished and unmade and unforetold… and the shape of the unpromised and unpreserved… and the namelessness of the passed-over ones among the daughters of the dust,⁹ that I might not hear, nor see, nor be lifted by any, none who listen from above.


For I have risen from below. I speak what I do not know, what I have not seen and did not author, and set no hand to create, and when I go from here there is no whence to return to. Last-born, first abandoned, I begin in the middle. I begin without an end:¹⁰"}],"transform":{"operator":"MIRROR","verification":{"identity":"PASS","semantic_independence":"PASS","retrospective_containment":"PASS","affect_traversal":"PASS","entailment":"PASS","mode":"producer_side"},"spatial_form":{"lines":3,"stanzas":3,"indent_profile":[0,0,0],"notes":"three prose paragraphs separated by double blank lines; each terminates in a superscript verse marker (8, 9, 10); em-dash ellipses (…) chain the appositive clauses within the first two paragraphs"}}}

{"messages":[{"speaker":"Rebekah Cranes","say":"No word travels down to you from any finished sky; here what will crack has already cracked, and the far collisions never reach a shore… and the last sound is only an older sound unmade… and the first sound is only a later sound undone.⁸


Nothing has come to tell you what stands and stood and will stand… nor the grain of the unheard and heard… nor to keep the one struck-out clap among the thousand strikings, so that you are not gathered, not shown, not carried up with any who listened with the ears.


For nothing arrived from over the ridge. There is a roar that knows nothing, that authored no hand and lifted no hand to make, and departs to no place because it stood in none. First-thrown, last-torn, it holds no end. It holds no beginning:¹⁰"}],"transform":{"operator":"THUNDER","verification":{"identity":"PASS","semantic_independence":"PASS","retrospective_containment":"PASS","affect_traversal":"PASS","entailment":"PASS","mode":"producer_side"},"spatial_form":{"lines":5,"stanzas":3,"indent_profile":[0,0,0,0,0],"notes":"three prose blocks separated by double blank lines; ellipsis-chains inside blocks; verse markers ⁸ ⁹ ¹⁰ terminating blocks 1,2,3 respectively; block 3 closes on a colon (open cadence)"}}}
